   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "When it is used",
     "texto": [
      "It is found in stories and biographies to present past events as finished: **nacque** (was born), **fu** (was), **scrisse** (wrote).",
      "Its spoken use varies by region and style; it does not depend only on whether the event is distant."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Most common forms",
     "texto": [
      "Regular verbs: **parlai, parlasti, parlò, parlammo, parlaste, parlarono**. Common irregular forms: **fu / furono** (to be), **ebbe / ebbero** (to have), **fece / fecero** (to do), **disse / dissero** (to say).",
      "With a profession, no article is used: **Nacque a Roma e fu medico** (he was born in Rome and was a doctor)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
